<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Go-Toba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1180">1180</a>–1239</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Go-Toba was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1183 to 1198 and then ruled as retired emperor. Seeking to restore imperial power, he raised forces against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jokyu-war">Jokyu War</a> of 1221 but was defeated by the Hojo regents and exiled to the Oki Islands, where he died. He was a leading poet and commissioned the Shin Kokinshu anthology.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-go-toba.jpg" alt="Emperor Go-Toba" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fujiwara no Nobuzane · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Go-Toba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
